{"_v":1,"id":"fela-2009","cat":"broadway","cs":83.48,"rc":7,"bd":{"positive":7,"mixed":0,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Jennifer Farrar","o":"Associated Press","s":91,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.newstimes.com/entertainment/article/Review-Fela-dance-party-finds-its-way-to-B-way-262086.php","d":"2009-11-23","q":"\"Fela!\" is a unique Broadway experience that leaves the audience on their feet and wanting more."},{"cn":"David Cote","o":"Time Out New York","s":89,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/newyork/theater/fela","d":"2009-11-24","q":"Fela! is more than a musical; it's an ecstatic phenomenon."},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":83,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2009/legit/reviews/fela-3-1200477297/","d":"2009-11-23","q":"Such reservations are secondary to the tremendous raw authenticity and electric energy of this dance-heavy bio-musical, and the dangerous sensuality of Sahr Ngaujah, who inhabits the title role with a cool command that never loses intensity."},{"cn":"Michael Billington","o":"The Guardian","s":79,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://www.guardian.co.uk/stage/2010/nov/17/fela-review","d":"2010-11-17","q":"The dancing is ecstatic, the music lifts the spirits, and the stage is alive with movement."},{"cn":"Elisabeth Vincentelli","o":"New York Post","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.nypost.com/p/entertainment/theater/plenty_of_afro_heat_kQGx3P1vFBYrLx0bbPQ1VK","d":"2009-09-24","q":"This is as close as Broadway gets to fully immersive theater."},{"cn":"Elysa Gardner","o":"USA Today","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.usatoday.com/life/theater/reviews/2009-11-24-fela24_st_N.htm","d":"2009-11-23","q":"Fela! earns its exclamation point, joyfully and relentlessly."},{"cn":"Michael Sommers","o":"New Jersey Newsroom","s":76,"b":"Positive","t":3,"u":"https://www.newjerseynewsroom.com/movies/afrobeat-music-drives-broadways-new-fela","d":"2009-11-23","q":"Broadway has never before witnessed a musical quite like \"Fela!\" — an explosive mix of catchy Afrobeat rhythms, wild, sexy dancing and raw bio-dramatics — and while its unique charms certainly are powerful, one frankly wonders whether this unusual show will catch on with the mainstream public."}],"au":{"score":63,"designation":"Disliking","sources":{"mz":{"s":63,"c":26,"sr":3.2}}},"tn":[{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Choreography","n":"Bill T. Jones","w":true},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Costume Design of a Musical","n":"Marina Draghici","w":true},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Sound Design of a Musical","n":"Robert Kaplowitz","w":true},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Musical","n":null},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Book of a Musical","n":"Jim Lewis"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Book of a Musical","n":"Bill T. Jones"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Actor in a Musical","n":"Sahr Ngaujah"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Featured Actress in a Musical","n":"Lillias White"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Direction of a Musical","n":"Bill T. Jones"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Orchestrations","n":"Aaron Johnson"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Scenic Design of a Musical","n":"Marina Draghici"},{"yr":64,"cat":"Best Lighting Design of a Musical","n":"Robert Wierzel"}],"cn":{"t":"Critics celebrate \"Fela!\" as an electrifying, immersive theatrical experience that transforms Broadway into a joyous dance party, praising its infectious Afrobeat music and the show's ability to break down barriers between stage and audience.","rc":10},"bo":{"tw":null,"at":{"g":27110350,"p":416,"a":355451}},"ta":"230 W 49th St, New York, NY 10019","vs":{"sl":3,"so":4,"co":3,"am":4,"fa":3},"pd":"2009-10-19","ca":[{"n":"Kevin Mambo","r":"Fela Anikulapo-Kuti"},{"n":"Sahr Ngaujah","r":"Fela Anikulapo-Kuti"},{"n":"Saycon Sengbloh","r":"Sandra"},{"n":"Lillias White","r":"Funmilayo"},{"n":"Anne V. Andre","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Corey Baker","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Hettie Vyrine Barnhill","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Lauren De Veaux","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Nicole Chantal de Weever","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Rujeko Dumbutshena","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Rasaan Elijah \"Talu\" Green","